data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_08865a3a69524928006a7bae47cee88195a1d8f9b64d076966","logprobs":[],"output_index":2,"sequence_number":308,"text":"Here are the most recent notable updates about NASA’s Mars Perseverance rover (from NASA/JPL and related coverage):\n\n- **Perseverance imaged Earth disappearing behind Mars’ moon Phobos (Aug 5, 2026):** The rover captured a sequence showing **Earth as a small bright dot** moving and then **vanishing behind Phobos** in the Martian sky—an unusual “occultation” style observation from the surface of Mars. 【5:1†source】【5:4†source】\n\n- **Perseverance “completed a marathon” of driving on Mars (reported July 14, 2026):** NASA announced the rover has now driven the equivalent of **26.2 miles (42.195 km)** on Mars. An orbital image from **Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter/HiRISE** showed the rover and its tracks across the terrain. 【5:0†source】\n\n- **Earlier 2026 milestone: first AI-planned drives on another world (Jan 30, 2026 / Feb 2, 2026 coverage):** Perseverance executed drives whose routes were **planned by a vision-capable generative AI system** (generating waypoints), a test led by JPL to reduce reliance on human route planning and improve autonomy. 【5:3†source】【5:2†source】\n\nIf you tell me whether you care more about **science findings** (rocks/samples), **new imagery**, or **tech milestones**, I can summarize the latest items in that category specifically."}

